        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1b74464e-6126-511b-98fd-363c2c84f41a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: New Hampshire Route 118, Woodstock, Canaan, White Mountains Region, Upper Valley region, Cushman, Berlin, Maine border, Dorchester, New Hampshire, Dorchester Common Historic District\n- Organizations: Dorchester Community Church\n- Buildings: town hall\n- Topics: regional boundaries, historic sites\n\nFacts:\n- New Hampshire Route 118 stretches from Woodstock in the White Mountains Region south to Canaan in the Upper Valley region.\n- The northern boundary of the White Mountains Region begins at Cushman, runs to Berlin, and then continues east to the Maine border.\n- The Dorchester Community Church is a historic church building located off New Hampshire Route 118 in Dorchester, New Hampshire.\n- The Dorchester Community Church was built in 1828 in the Dorchester Common Historic District.\n- A town hall was built in 1844 in the Dorchester Common Historic District on the site of Dorchester's first town hall from 1828.",
